    "['encapsulation source-address [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 encapsulation source-address 5::5', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nsegment-routing ipv6 locator as1 encapsulation source-address 5::5\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact equivalent may vary slightly depending on Cisco IOS XE/IOS XR versions. The above translation assumes Cisco's Segment Routing IPv6 implementation where the source address is specified under the locator configuration. Some Cisco versions might use slightly different syntax like:\\n```\\nsegment-routing srv6\\n locator as1\\n  encapsulation source-address 5::5\\n```\\nBut the core functionality remains the same - specifying the SRv6 encapsulation source address.\", 'trans_template': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 encapsulation source-address 5::5'}]]": 1,
    "['locator [parameter1] ipv6-prefix [parameter2] [parameter3] static [parameter4]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix 2001:DB8:15::/64 static 32', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nsegment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix 2001:DB8:15::/64 static 32\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei command `locator as1 ipv6-prefix 2001:db8:15:: 64 static 32` defines an SRv6 locator with:\\n  - Locator name: as1\\n  - IPv6 prefix: 2001:db8:15::/64\\n  - Static SID allocation range of 32 bits\\n- The Cisco equivalent uses similar syntax but with:\\n  - `segment-routing ipv6 locator` prefix instead of just `locator`\\n  - The keyword `prefix` instead of `ipv6-prefix`\\n  - Note that Cisco typically uses uppercase for IPv6 addresses in configuration', 'trans_template': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix 2001:DB8:15::/64 static 32'}]]": 1,
    "['opcode [parameter1] end', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid index 1', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]', 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix 2001:DB8:15::/64 static 32'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nsegment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid index 1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei `opcode ::1 end` command assigns a static SID (Segment Identifier) with value ::1 and marks it as an \"end\" SID (which represents the router itself in SRv6).\\n- The Cisco equivalent uses `prefix-sid index` to assign a SID index value (1 in this case) under the SRv6 locator configuration.\\n- The \"end\" behavior is implicit in Cisco\\'s implementation when assigning a prefix SID to the router\\'s locator.', 'trans_template': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid index 1'}]]": 1,
    "['opcode [parameter1] end-dt4 vpn-instance [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing local-block 2001:db8:15::/64', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]', 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix 2001:DB8:15::/64 static 32'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Huawei `opcode ::100 end-dt4 vpn-instance vpna` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nsegment-routing local-block 2001:db8:15::/64\\nsegment-routing prefix 2001:db8:15::100/128 vrf vpna\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei command defines an End.DT4 SID (::100) for IPv4 VPN (vpna) in the SRv6 locator\\n- In Cisco, this is translated to:\\n  1. First defining the local SID block (equivalent to Huawei's locator)\\n  2. Then mapping the specific SID (::100) to the VRF for IPv4 VPN functionality (End.DT4 equivalent)\\n- The Cisco implementation uses separate commands to achieve the same functionality\", 'trans_template': 'segment-routing local-block 2001:db8:15::/64'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing prefix 2001:db8:15::100/128 vrf vpna', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]', 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix 2001:DB8:15::/64 static 32'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Huawei `opcode ::100 end-dt4 vpn-instance vpna` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nsegment-routing local-block 2001:db8:15::/64\\nsegment-routing prefix 2001:db8:15::100/128 vrf vpna\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei command defines an End.DT4 SID (::100) for IPv4 VPN (vpna) in the SRv6 locator\\n- In Cisco, this is translated to:\\n  1. First defining the local SID block (equivalent to Huawei's locator)\\n  2. Then mapping the specific SID (::100) to the VRF for IPv4 VPN functionality (End.DT4 equivalent)\\n- The Cisco implementation uses separate commands to achieve the same functionality\", 'trans_template': 'segment-routing prefix 2001:db8:15::100/128 vrf vpna'}]]": 1,
